answer:
  title: What is a Yelp Advertising Partner?
  body: >-
    A Yelp Advertising Partner is an agency Yelp has certified to buy and manage
    Yelp advertising for clients. Partners complete Yelp's training, pass its
    compliance standards, and get access to partner tools, dedicated support, and
    client promotions that are not available to self-serve advertisers.
    Certification is granted by Yelp and reviewed on an ongoing basis.
  requiresTitle: What the program requires
  requires:
    - Complete Yelp's partner training course
    - Demonstrate a standard of client service Yelp is willing to put its name on
    - Meet Yelp's compliance guidelines on reviews and platform usage
    - Pass Yelp's periodic compliance checks to keep the status

plain:
  title: In plain terms
  subtitle: Why the program exists at all
  body:
    - >-
      Yelp worked out something most platforms take years to admit: a salesperson
      who meets a business once cannot serve it as well as an agency that already
      works with it every week.
    - >-
      A Yelp sales representative is handling a long list of accounts, is measured
      on new spend, and meets your business at the moment of the pitch. An agency
      that already runs the website, the listings and the reviews knows what a job
      is worth to you, which services are worth promoting this season, and what
      the phone is doing. Yelp cannot know any of that. The agency already does.
    - >-
      So rather than growing a bigger sales and account resolution team, Yelp
      built a program that hands campaign management, budget decisions and support
      to agencies who hold those relationships already, and pays them out of its
      own margin to do it well. That is the bet: an account looked after by
      someone with the full picture spends more sensibly, performs better, and
      stays on the platform longer than one sold in a phone call.
  cards:
    - who: The business gets
      what: Someone who knows the account making the call, and no cold pitch to evaluate alone.
    - who: The agency gets
      what: Tools, support and a rebate, so it is paid to keep the campaign working rather than to sell it once.
    - who: Yelp gets
      what: Advertisers who stay, because the campaigns produce work instead of being cancelled in month three.

