cost:
  eyebrow: Plainly stated
  title: Does working with a Yelp Partner cost more?
  lede: >-
    Three facts, stated separately, because they pull in different directions and
    every one of them is true. Two of them are in your favour. The third is what
    we charge, and it belongs on the page next to the other two rather than in a
    footnote.
  facts:
    - label: Fact one
      title: Yelp pays certified partners a rebate on the ad spend they manage
      body: >-
        It is based on client spend under management and it comes out of Yelp's
        side, not out of your budget. You should know it exists before you hire
        anyone, and any partner who will not answer that question directly is the
        wrong partner.
    - label: Fact two
      title: Partner clients get pricing self-serve advertisers cannot reach
      body: >-
        Bundled pricing, free upgrades and ad credits are available through
        partners and not on the self-serve dashboard. New advertisers frequently
        qualify for a matched-spend window running about six months, which on
        accounts we have opened has been worth more than a thousand dollars of
        placement. It is available once.
    - label: Fact three
      title: Circulation Studio charges a fee on top of ad spend
      body: >-
        Our fee is separate from what you pay Yelp, and it is published below
        rather than quoted on a call. It is a one-time setup and optimization fee
        to start, and ongoing ad management carries no monthly fee. Review
        management is the one recurring item, and only if you want it.
  close: >-
    We read the account before we quote it: category, market, review position and
    what a job is worth to you. If the numbers do not support it, we say so and
    stop there. An account that cannot succeed is worth nothing to us either, and
    it costs us more to manage a losing campaign than to decline it.
  cta: See what we charge

